const CHANGES=[
  ['1.7',[
    'Seven new themes -- Dracula, Amphora, Marble, Steel, Glass, Neon, Wood -- alongside the five you already had, twelve in all. Two have their own material: Glass is frosted and translucent, Neon glows.',
    'The theme picker is now a grid of real previews, each showing its own light and dark side by side, with a bigger preview of your current theme above it -- rather than a row of plain colour dots.',
    'The calendar now colours each day by how much you studied, instead of two small hard-to-read numbers -- a toggle switches it to colour by how well you recalled instead, and a gear icon lets you change the accent colour and how many days it averages against. An "All-time" view sits alongside the month view.',
    'The three wide-screen study switches (review history, keyboard hints, animation) are now one Full/Simplified choice in Settings, instead of three separate ones.',
    'A well-known word now moves on properly the moment you get it right -- until now, a Good rating on a new word could be held back for several tries before it actually advanced, with Easy as the only real way through.'
  ]],
  ['1.6',[
    'The word list now has a + button to add a word by hand, and an i button on any word to correct a typo in it or, for a word you added yourself, delete it.',
    'A live clock while studying, and two new lines under Timing on the home screen: how long you have actually studied today and over the last week, and the typical time it takes to learn a new word.',
    'A new button on the Riverbank home screen exports a backup of every language you have used on this device, in one tap.',
    'Settings, the Guide, and What\'s new moved from the home screen\'s card list to small icons at the top, next to the title -- the list below is languages only now.',
    'This device now asks the browser to keep its data safe from automatic clearing, the same protection installed apps already had.',
    'Sync is more resilient to a dropped connection: a rating in the last few seconds is no longer lost if you close the tab right after; a failed sync says so more clearly; and what gets sent is now compressed, so a large backup uses less data.'
  ]],
  ['1.5',[
    'Fixed the two-column layout on wide screens and tablets sometimes landing badly uneven -- one column visibly taller than the other on Home and Settings.',
    'Removed the "Unlock the reverse direction after" setting -- unused (confirmed against real usage data) and no longer configurable.',
    'A failed sync now says more clearly whether it is your connection or something on the synced copy itself.'
  ]],
  ['1.0',[
    'First release. Forked from vocabula\'s FSRS study engine, with a smaller settings page: hesitation-adjusted grading, easy-only clearing and the 3-day drill release are always on rather than switchable, and there is no known-word head start since every word here starts unseen.',
    'Backup and sync no longer needs a GitHub account. Get a short code in Settings, type the same code into another device, and both stay in step. The code doubles as an encryption key, so anything sent between devices is unreadable in transit and at rest.',
    'Five themes instead of seven, chosen to look distinct from each other at a glance rather than to cover every palette.'
  ]],
  ['1.1',[
    'A proper layout for tablets, laptops, and a phone turned sideways: a two-pane study screen, a redesigned home screen, and two-column Settings.',
    'Fixed a brief flash when revealing an answer on Safari.',
    'Opt-in, anonymous usage stats you can turn on in Settings — never your name, device, or word content.'
  ]],
  ['1.2',[
    'One sync code now works across every language, instead of needing a separate one for each.'
  ]],
  ['1.3',[
    'Fixed a bug that could let a single review loop back on itself indefinitely in one sitting instead of settling after a few tries.',
    'General security hardening under the hood.',
    'Renamed the "Secret" theme to "Smoo"; finding it again now takes the tap sequence each visit instead of unlocking it permanently.',
    'Device name, theme, and a few other personal settings now carry over automatically between languages.'
  ]],
  ['1.4',[
    'Wide-screen study extras (review history, keyboard hints, animation) and your sync code now live on one shared Settings page from the home screen, applying to all four languages at once.',
    'The reverse direction now unlocks immediately by default, instead of after two weeks.',
    'Removed the "study day begins at" setting — the day always resets at 4am now.'
  ]]
];
